         Fix an allocation leak in the HTTP/2 backlog tracking when a stream is
         reset. (markt)
       </fix>
+      <fix>
+        <bug>70236</bug>: Fix a stalled TLS handshake with the OpenSSL based
+        implementations of <code>SSLEngine</code> when the first flight of
+        handshake messages sent by the server is too large to fit in the
+        buffer used by the BIO pair. This typically requires a large
+        certificate chain. Once the buffer has been drained by
+        <code>wrap()</code>, give OpenSSL the opportunity to write the
+        remainder of the flight rather than waiting for the client to send
+        data it will not send until it has received that flight. Patch
+        submitted by Lukas Hellebrandt. (markt)
+      </fix>
     </changelog>
